WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.086 --> 00:00:04.211
- As long as prosthesis have been around,

00:00:04.211 --> 00:00:05.280
people have been really focusing

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.160
on making it look like a
hand and move like a hand,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.909
but a hand is not just a grabber.

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:12.409
A hand is a touch.

00:00:14.219 --> 00:00:16.568
It's touch that engages
you with the world.

00:00:16.568 --> 00:00:19.597
It's touch that engages you with people.

00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:21.987
A prosthesis without touch is a tool.

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.487
By giving touch, we're giving back a hand.

00:00:29.835 --> 00:00:34.725
- I worked in a factory
setting before I lost my arm.

00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:37.576
I was doing some cleaning
out from underneath

00:00:37.576 --> 00:00:40.488
a shredder-type machine,
and it grabbed the material

00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:44.655
that was in my hand and pulled
my hand into the machine.

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:49.019
I didn't think that I'd ever
have the sensation of touch

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:50.907
or anything back again,

00:00:50.907 --> 00:00:53.605
and then my prosthetist told me about the

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:56.165
research program up here in Cleveland.

00:00:56.165 --> 00:01:00.332
They hope to be able to
give me the sense of touch.

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:03.824
- The research that we've been doing

00:01:03.824 --> 00:01:05.865
is reconnecting the man to the machine.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:09.424
Basically, learning how to
take what the prosthesis feels

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:13.603
and translates so that the
person using it feels it.

00:01:13.603 --> 00:01:16.944
For the brain to feel touch
as being their actual hand,

00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:19.493
it's really important that
we activate or stimulate the

00:01:19.493 --> 00:01:24.053
wires that the brain always
used to get from the hand.

00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:27.093
What we do is we implant cuff
electrodes and then we apply

00:01:27.093 --> 00:01:30.493
really tiny amounts of current
that activate those wires,

00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:32.264
and that information
then goes to the brain.

00:01:32.264 --> 00:01:35.633
So we've been learning how
to place this information

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:39.955
on that nerve, so the
brain thinks it's his hand.

00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:42.302
They can feel not just
buzzing, but also a touch,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.453
a pressure, like somebody
putting a finger on their hand.

00:01:44.453 --> 00:01:46.965
And in fact, we've been
able to see that intensity

00:01:46.965 --> 00:01:51.132
of the artificial stimulation
mimics the intact hand.

00:01:54.275 --> 00:01:56.163
- Soft big block.

00:01:56.163 --> 00:01:59.232
The first time they put
sensation on and everything,

00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:01.389
it was just incredible.

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:02.751
It was like, "Wow."

00:02:02.751 --> 00:02:06.104
Could actually feel an area
in my hand, a certain area,

00:02:06.104 --> 00:02:09.824
tingling, and vibrations, and stuff.

00:02:09.824 --> 00:02:11.675
Small soft block.

00:02:11.675 --> 00:02:14.592
I said, just an incredible feeling.

00:02:16.747 --> 00:02:19.307
Bringing the prosthetic home
with the sensory hand on it

00:02:19.307 --> 00:02:21.317
and being able to feel and everything's

00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:24.053
changed life considerably.

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:28.613
It's just little things that
people take for granted.

00:02:28.613 --> 00:02:31.232
Brushing teeth, to be able
to hold the toothpaste

00:02:31.232 --> 00:02:33.809
and be able to squeeze and
tell how hard I'm squeezing it

00:02:33.809 --> 00:02:36.541
so I don't squeeze it
and it go everyplace.

00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:39.240
It makes it a lot easier.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.960
- We're at the point where
subjects can use their prosthesis

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.008
at home, and they can have
sensation while they're at home.

00:02:44.008 --> 00:02:45.490
It makes them two-handed again.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.407
It brings back their
hand, it makes them whole.

